'' AN IIF INSIDE A STRING CONCATENATION, in a function returning a string or a UDT holding
'' one, compiles, links and runs. The concat term path sent EVERY iif to the STRING iif --
'' "the destination is a string, so an iif here is a string iif whatever its arms look
'' like" -- and a numeric arm could not become a descriptor. LowerStringIif_ returned
'' AFTER branching, with the builder left in the THEN arm, so the function's own RETURN
'' was emitted there and the other path fell to 'ret void': clang refused the module,
'' "value doesn't match function result type 'ptr'". --dump-ir said '0 statements not
'' lowered'.
''
'' Now an iif whose arms are typed SCALARS -- numbers, floats, booleans, enums, pointers
'' -- is rendered as the value it is (IifArmsScalar_), as fbc does; untyped and string
'' arms keep the string iif. And a string iif that cannot finish an arm leaves a
'' well-formed function (StrIifAbandon_): the statement declines where it can be seen.
''
'' MEASURED, fbc-modern 1.20: the source prints, byte for byte, what fbc's build prints
'' (see its header). A DRIVER TEST BECAUSE IT HAS TO LINK -- the failure was clang's; the
'' source is a goldenrun.sh differential too.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -i toolchains/tiko-windows/inc tests/driver/src/iif-in-concat.bas -o tests/driver/iifinconcat.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/iifinconcat.exe
